  "body": "User-agent-controlled credentials are only included for matching requests, but developer-controlled credentials will be copied from request to request.\r\n\r\nThere's a proposal to scope a developer-controlled `Authorization` header to the origin of the initial request. (If you use other headers to carry credentials you are out of luck.)\r\n\r\nThis might be reasonably compatible as `Authorization` is a header that requires a preflight (and does not allow wildcards) and redirects for preflights were not followed until recently.\r\n\r\nWhat's needed to move this forward:\r\n\r\n - [x] Implementers need to be interested.\r\n - [x] Tests need to be written to ensure it's dropped at the appropriate time (and other headers are not).\r\n - [x] The specification needs to be updated to account for this. Perhaps by reusing https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#cors-non-wildcard-request-header-name somehow.\r\n\r\ncc @whatwg/security ",
